WEBVTT

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:14.750
It's said that if you go there,
any dream can come true.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.120
I know. Let's go to Isekandar.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.160
"I know. Let's go to Isekandar."
I know. Let's go to Isekandar.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.950
"I know. Let's go to Isekandar."

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.700
Ooh, so this is the last checkpoint.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.450
Let's head on in like nothing's wrong.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.700
Please transmit your passport code.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.500
Hmm, and if this gets kicked back to us,
we break through like we're hoping to.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.450
That's conceivable.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.870
Confirmed. Passage approved.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.080
Huh?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.200
We're through!

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.500
That's unexpected!

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.370
Did they not check very hard?

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.160
Everything turned out all right.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.450
Yeah, yeah!

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.790
We're about to arrive at Isekandar!
We're finally here, Hatchi!

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.040
Yep.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.410
Yes!

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.700
Let's get our hands on some Akafucrystals

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.500
and find happiness!

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.000
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.700
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.700
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.250
"At last, they've reached Isekandar,
planet of happiness"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.120
"It seemed to take so long, yet was so short"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.450
"But any longer than this and
the studio would kick us out (aww)"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.120
"But any longer than this and
the studio would kick us out (aww)"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.000
"Common Fame Is a Common Isekandar"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.200
We're here!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.290
After wanting so badly for so long
to get here, we're here!

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.910
The world of happiness, Isekandar!

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.370
That didn't take as long as I thought it would.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:02.450
Yeah, maybe. But we also ran into a lot
of hard times along the way, didn't we?

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.620
But those are about to come to an end.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.250
We'll get our hands on some
Akafucrystals and begin a happy life.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.910
--Huh?
--What?

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:18.080
The things I thought were
planetary rings circling Isekandar

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.000
are all a bunch of ads.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.580
For real?

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:27.160
An awesome number of ads.
Isekandar is shamelessly commercial.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.290
Is this really a miracle world?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.950
It's just a bunch of companies wanting
to share Isekandar's good fortune.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.000
Putting ads where people
gather is basic marketing.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.330
How cool!

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.040
It must be a real power spot!

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.200
I'm telling you, they're just ads.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.450
Yahoo!

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.330
We've arrived on Isekandar!

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.580
So that's the sacred mountain Akafuji,

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.120
where the giant Akafucrystal is enshrined.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.040
The Great Temple of Isekandar is there.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.450
There's a convention
to follow when visiting it.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:07.160
You take the approach path
early in the morning.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.660
We'll have to spend
the night somewhere first.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.580
We can't afford to waste money,
so sleep on the <i>Nagaya Voyager</i>!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.120
As long as we're here, let's stay at an inn.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.120
There are all kinds here,
from modern to traditional.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.580
I'd prefer something with a strong local flavor.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:24.080
--This is nice, too, right?
--Nah, <i>that </i>one.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.410
--Hey, we've only just landed on Isekandar;
our luck hasn't changed yet!
--Nah, <i>that </i>one.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.330
--Hey, we've only just landed on Isekandar;
our luck hasn't changed yet!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.290
Look at all these people.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.700
Mm-hmm.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.620
Look at this! There are signboards
written in Earth language!

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.160
Shows you how many sightseers
they get from Earth.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.790
I'm telling you, this place is booming.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:46.330
Isekan udon! How about some
of the local specialty Isekan udon?

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.870
Isekan udon!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.160
Guess we could eat.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.330
You just barely ate breakfast!

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.830
Isekan canes! Take an
Isekan cane on your visit!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.870
Cool! Isekan canes!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.160
They'll make nice keepsakes.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.950
They'll just clutter the place up afterward!

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.620
Fortune slips here!

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.040
We don't need them! Stop!

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.200
What is it?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.370
You've already drawn them!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.500
A wonderful encounter is in store.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:16.080
Conduct yourself however you wish.
Do not skimp on your offering. Average luck.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.450
Waver not away from major ways mayonnaise.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:23.750
Great luck! Ah! It has a discount
coupon for Isekan <i>manju </i>buns!

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.660
You sure are lucky.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.700
Want to trade?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.540
Is this something that
trading will even affect?

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:34.290
Who knows? But you're the one
who wants better luck, so...

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:37.290
Heh, I appreciate the offer, anyway.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:41.330
Once I get an Akafucrystal,
my luck is going to change.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:44.000
Then stop wasting money and hurry on ahead.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.290
Let's get a photo!

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.500
Stop! Let me go!

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.910
A memento, a memento!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.620
You almost never see Isekangaroos in photos.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.830
Smile, smile!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.450
Wow, everywhere you go,
it's wall-to-wall souvenir vendors.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:02.080
That's how it always is outside a temple gate.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.450
It's nice and fun, isn't it?

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:08.410
"Isefuku"
Come to Isefuku! Come to Isefuku
to drive away your evil spirits!

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.330
Drive away evil?

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.620
"The Original Isefuku"
Choose the original Isefuku
for your cloistering needs!

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.000
Cloistering?

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.160
Cloister at the original Isefuku!

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.910
Just 50 bues and 5000 mons for the set!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.790
Fifty bues, 5000 mons?

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.000
Like hell it's a cloister! Any way
you look at it, it's a cabaret club!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.950
Ward off evil at the original Isefuku!

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.580
"New Isefuku"
Main Isefuku location, this way!

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.870
"New Isefuku"
Flagship Isefuku location here!

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.660
"New Isefuku"
Come to the New Isefuku!

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.950
The kind of imitation shops
you tend to see in any tourist spot.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.580
<i>That's </i>what you're going to comment on?

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.700
You're okay with cabaret clubs
being at the temple's gate?

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.040
Lots of great girls here!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.660
Which one should I choose?

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:41.660
Hey, Robby!

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.370
I won't be long, I'll be real quick.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:47.620
Okay, I'll be waiting for you while eating
good-luck Isekan <i>manju </i>buns.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.750
You're not gonna stop him?

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.000
Whoa, that's bad.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.580
It got good reviews on TripSunvisor,
though. Well, whatever.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.580
Are you sure about this?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.250
The trip is almost over,
and I thought I'd enjoy myself.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.700
You're homesick?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.370
No, it's not that.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.750
Oh?

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.450
Sorry to keep you.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.080
But I wrapped things up
without any extensions.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.450
I'm sure you were offered
some fruit or something

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.910
and had your money swindled away.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:24.660
Oh, shut up! Come on, let's go.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.160
Ah! A sacred bird, the Akafu jack!

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.080
Sacred bird?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.040
It's a bird of fortune that extends your life
a hundred days if you pray to it.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.500
Really? We have to pray!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.370
Whoever said such a thing?!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.290
Let's stay here tonight.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:43.500
We're really staying the night?
This is what you get for dragging your feet.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.330
It's the custom for visitors.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.330
What do you mean, custom?

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:51.120
You spend the night before you
make your visit to cleanse yourself.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.410
It's supposedly called "Oharaitown."

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.580
You're sure they're not just shaking down
the visitors for more money?

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:01.200
Ikku, you've been pretty skeptical
since we got to Isekandar, haven't you?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:05.040
I'm a robot. I'm not equipped
with any sense of faith,

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.410
so I just call them like I see them.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:10.750
Then you could have just waited
aboard the <i>Nagaya Voyager</i>, right?

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.620
I don't believe in God or miracles.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.950
But I want to see this giant
Akafucrystal for myself,

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:20.950
and scientifically learn what
it's made of, and what power it has.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:23.160
Hey, let's spend the night over there.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.080
Hey! Don't ignore me!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.540
"Isekan Hollow"

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:31.950
Cleanse yourself! Cleanse yourself!

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.700
Purify the hell out of your
polluted mind and body!

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.410
At last, this is starting to feel
more like a pilgrimage.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:56.500
It sure is a long way to the summit.
Oh! A sacred Akafu jack!

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.200
How about it?

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.870
More grist for the mill.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.750
You're wasting more money!

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:04.870
We're almost there.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.620
Ooh, it's so majestic!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.910
That is all the room we have
for the group at this time.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.410
Please wait for the next group.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.830
They take us in shifts?

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.540
Lucky us. We don't have to wait to get in.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.540
My luck is already starting to change!

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.870
Behold!

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.620
There it is! The sacred giant Akafucrystal!

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:35.120
It's even huger than I imagined!

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.120
We should take a photo
to remember this by, too.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.620
What's this?

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:49.000
I am Spacia of Isekandar,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.620
priestess of the Great Temple of Isekandar.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:55.330
Priestesses are the best, huh?

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.330
Hey, stop your drooling!

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.620
Miss priestess!

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.500
Hey! Don't ignore me!

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:06.040
I pray for all of your good fortune.
May you be profited!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.750
Exercise your faith.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:15.660
Make others' joy your own joy.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.750
Do so, and good fortune
will befall you in due course.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.910
Now, please proceed inside.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.790
Offerings over here, if you please.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.160
Your offerings are accepted here.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.040
This way to give your offerings.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:33.160
Do you think 10,000 mons will be enough?

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:34.450
Sure, why not?

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.450
I'm not giving them one red mon.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:39.080
Ten thousand mons? Very well, here you go.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:40.870
This is an Akafucrystal!

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:43.950
All right! I finally got my hands on one!

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.660
Now I can obtain good fortune!

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.500
Way to go!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.620
Huh? Didn't they say the Akafucrystals

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.000
were supposed to come in
some kind of special bag?

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.580
That's just a regular paper bag, right?

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:00.580
Unfortunately, that promotion
ended yesterday.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.870
Huh?!

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:05.620
The benefits don't take hold
unless you put it in its special bag.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.040
They don't?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.950
Benefits, schmenefits.
You'll fall for anything they say.

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:12.870
Get your Isekangaroo pouches!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:16.660
Isekangaroo pouches to put your
Akafucrystals into, over here!

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.370
Isekangaroo pouches!

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:22.410
Miss, you sell Isekangaroo pouches here?!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:26.450
Yes. Isekangaroo pouches made from
all-natural materials are right here.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.790
The also include an original print.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.750
All-natural-material Isekangaroo pouches!

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.200
Yes. Over there.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.950
Huh? Are they real?

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:38.330
Yes.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.790
Those are real Isekangaroos!

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:46.910
They sure are tame. They aren't
running away at all. Hmm?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.620
Is that...?

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.250
Does this mean that Isekangaroo pouches...

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:55.120
Yes, that's correct. When you place
your Akafucrystal into this pouch,

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.330
good fortune will come to you.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.620
Isekangaroo pouches, eh?

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.870
My legs! I can walk again!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.080
Grandpa!

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.370
--It's a miracle!
--It's a miracle!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.290
It's a miracle!

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:06.830
I'm so glad we came!

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:09.620
Whoa, that's awesome!

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.540
A rare metal ore deposit!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.790
You found one at last! Way to go!

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.080
--It's a miracle!
--It's a miracle!

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.200
It's a miracle!

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.580
Wicked awesome!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.700
Wicked fishy.

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.290
But it looks like it's for real.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.450
Not you, too!

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:23.750
Miss, one pouch, please!

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.160
Sure. We have small, medium, or large.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.120
One for these.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:28.330
Small it is.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:30.950
--Huh?
--One large, please.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:35.000
Very good, sir! You are sure
to be greatly profited!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.000
That's because of our huge contribution.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.250
When you consider the benefits,
100,000 mons was a bargain for this.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.870
It's hopeless.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:47.910
Money is the key that
opens all doors, I guess.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.080
All right,

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.830
if that's how it's gonna be...

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.700
After all the work it took
to come to Isekandar,

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.950
I'm not gonna give up now and
go back to my life of poverty!

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.370
No matter what, no matter what,

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:07.120
I'm gonna get me that Akafucrystal!

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.910
What do you suppose he plans
to do with that hammer?

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.160
Who knows?

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:15.790
But the way Robby's mind works,
it's probably nothing good.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:19.000
I'm gonna be happy! I'm gonna be rich!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.450
I'm gonna get greater fortune than anyone!

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:23.450
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:24.450
Thievery?!

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.290
This is how badly you
want to find happiness?!

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.950
Robby has become a criminal!

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.330
Robby, you may be dumb,
but you were a good guy.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.080
What is this?

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:45.080
Huh? What is that?

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:48.160
Hmm...

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.660
This is some kind of polymer.
Polycarbonate or something.

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:53.290
It's supposed to be natural stone.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.540
Who says that?

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:56.250
TripSunvisor.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.660
Okay...

00:13:58.790 --> 00:13:59.540
Robby!

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:00.500
What's the big idea!?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.620
I'm gonna see this with my own eyes!

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.290
<i>What </i>are you gonna see?!

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.700
First thievery, now trespassing?

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.160
Though that sounds like fun,
so I'm coming along.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.790
What the hell! First it's a pilgrimage,
now it's spelunking?!

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.160
What is this place?

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:20.500
Why is there a hallway
in the middle of this cliff?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.080
It looks like a hidden base.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.540
I doubt it's anything so grandiose.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:28.540
Akafucrystal lighting! Switch on!

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:29.370
What was that?

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:31.000
Shh! Let's see.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.000
That's the pair we met on Pluto!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.250
The ones from the major advertising agency.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:40.870
Kodai, when can we ever go back to Earth?

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:45.120
I can't believe we were demoted
back here after the debacle on Pluto!

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:47.540
The Isekandar operation
is our main enterprise.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.620
I'm telling you, it's not a demotion.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.370
What are they doing here?

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.000
Who knows?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:57.200
The rate of earnings on Okage Street
have dropped 0.5 points from yesterday.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:01.790
Souvenir sales in Oharaitown are
currently at 60% of target amount.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:06.000
Increase the turnover ratio! Release an
Akafu jack! Attract more visitors!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.160
They're analyzing the revenues.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.580
Launching Akafu Jack #2!

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:13.950
It's not a sacred bird, it's a drone.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.580
Miss Spacia, we're starting the
afternoon crowd 10 minutes early.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:20.450
Damn it, I can't take this! I demand a raise!

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.580
She isn't a priestess, she's an employee?

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.000
Okay, performers, it's almost time to go on.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.200
Are you ready to go on?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.700
Whenever you are!

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.040
They weren't miracles.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.540
They're all plants?

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:32.410
How's your husband been lately?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.950
Things are an absolute disaster
with our daughter-in-law.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.200
I hear chia seeds are supposed
to be good for that.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:41.750
Oh, yeah, their doctor won't prescribe
hardly anything, you know?

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:47.000
The miracle-working Akafucrystals are
mass-produced by gossipy old biddies.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.910
They're nothing but polymer resin.

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:52.000
There's a staff running the business
behind the scenes on Isekandar.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.870
Just like an amusement park.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:56.870
Any way you slice it, this is the
work of that major ad agency.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.660
Isekandar was... Isekandar was...

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.910
...an Ise-counterfeit all along!

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.580
Oh, my, are you boys from Dontsu?

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.410
Hmm? Dontsu?

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:07.660
And sure enough...

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:10.580
No, we aren't. We're visitors to the temple.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:13.290
Oh, dear, how did you get in here?

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.830
We believed--that is, I believed

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:18.540
that if I could get my hands on
an Akafucrystal from Isekandar,

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.290
then miraculous good fortune
would drop into my lap.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:27.200
Oh my word! You did what? You really
came to Isekandar in search of profit?

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:29.290
Ever since those Dontsu folks came here,

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.830
the whole place has been
turned into a tourist attraction.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:34.950
This has been one big
commercially-based campaign!

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.540
This entire pilgrimage to Isekandar!

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:42.870
There is an actual sacred
Akafucrystal, but it's so small.

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:45.290
Those Dontsu folks said
it was too unimpressive,

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.160
so they created this huge fake one
to draw in more crowds.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:51.950
And I believed the whole fairy tale... Hmm?

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:54.830
Those Isekangaroos aren't from here, either.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.330
--Those Dontsu folks brought them
in from some other planet.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.410
--What did you just say, ma'am?
--Those Dontsu folks brought them
in from some other planet.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.080
Huh? Isekangaroos aren't--

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.620
Not about that, about the
sacred crystal. There's a real one?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:09.200
Oh, my, you mean the one that us
local folks used to make pilgrimages to?

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.160
Yes, that, that! Where is it?!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.250
Go past where all those
kangaroos always gather--

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:14.910
Yes!

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:17.620
This time, I'm gonna find happiness for sure!

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:19.830
Thank you, ma'am! See you!

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:23.330
If you're going there,
watch out for wild kangaroos!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:25.540
--Wild?
--What kind of place is this?!

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.250
Robby isn't coming through, is he?

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:32.370
No, he's not.

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:39.870
Robby's debt has been paid in full!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.750
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:42.750
It can't be! So then...

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.450
...that means he passed through customs?!

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:48.410
Damn! How did he manage to get the money?!

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:51.290
We're going to Isekandar!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.830
--Hooray!
--Hooray!

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.040
I always wanted an Akafucrystal!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:58.580
Me, too! And those bags
are cute, aren't they?

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:02.450
Without a doubt, Robby is still on Isekandar.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:05.870
Is it really someplace this out of the way?

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:10.000
Well, at least it's more
authentic than all that clamor.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.950
Ah! There it is! There it is!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:16.700
This is it! A natural Akafucrystal!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.700
It's a far cry from the fake one.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.950
It does look like it has prosperity!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.250
So what are you gonna do?
Chip off a piece with a hammer again?

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:28.660
You idiot! Just try it! You'll get
smitten and chase all the luck away!

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.830
That didn't stop you from
chipping away at it earlier.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:34.290
Yeah, well, that was over
how much money you offered,

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:37.040
and I was just trying to get back
my 10,000 mons' worth.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.620
Though it turned out
not to be worth anything.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.040
You think I've earned any favor now?

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:50.290
If you think you have, then you have.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:54.370
All right, back to Earth to make a fortune!

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:58.540
Ow!

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:00.000
Robby!

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.750
And the first thing he does is trip on a rock.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:05.160
Tripping over something
is a sign of some kind of luck.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.200
I think I'll keep this
as a memento of Isekandar.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:15.620
So, what do we do now? Post the fact
that Isekandar is a sham on U-Chube?

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:19.000
Won't do any good. They'll just
use their enormous funds

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:20.910
to manipulate the information we put out.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:26.080
And if we file a claim against them,
they'll say "so what?" and that's that.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:32.830
However, the fact that we travelled
together to Isekandar will be the truth.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:37.200
Huh? Yeah. The truth.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.040
Robby! Where are you?!

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:46.830
Mr. Yang, Robby is one thing, but as long
as we're here on Isekandar anyway...

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.290
...let's see the sights of Isekandar!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.120
What did you say?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.250
Now that we're here, I want to go
visit the Great Temple of Isekandar,

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.660
which is said to bring happiness!

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:01.040
I also called my grandma out in the country

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:03.370
and told her I'd bring her an Akafucrystal!

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.700
So can we at least get some souvenirs?

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.950
Mr. Yang, I'm sure you want one, too, right?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.870
Ha! In that case,

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.330
we can just snag that one right now!

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:18.750
--Awesome!
--Awesome!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:23.290
I was once known as
"Crane Game Yang" at the arcade.

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:24.200
Oh...!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.250
You got it!

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.950
I am Spacia of Isekandar--

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:35.200
Huh?! The Akafucrystal!

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.790
The Akafucrystal is ours!

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:42.620
What is this? It's just
mechanically-rigged facade!

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:45.410
--Huh?! It's fake?!
--Huh?! It's fake?!

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:47.410
--What the hell?!
--They cheated us!

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:51.000
--It's fake!
--We want our money back!
--Everyone, please settle down-- Hey, watch it!

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.870
How could that Akafucrystal be phony?

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.790
What will I tell my grandma
out in the country?

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.950
Never mind about this now!
The only thing I want to get...

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.410
...is Robby!

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:07.250
Just for a minute! I just want to go
to the priestess café for a minute!

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.500
The priestesses are all fake, too, you know.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:14.580
That's okay. I know all too well
what kind of place this is now.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:17.410
I just want them to be
dressed like priestesses.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:19.910
So can I go to the priestess café?

00:21:19.910 --> 00:21:22.080
You'll lose all the good luck you've gained.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:25.080
Just the opposite! I'm going
there to <i>test </i>my luck!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:28.120
I think it's best if we got off
of Isekandar as soon as possible.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.370
Huh?

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:30.620
Over there.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:35.120
Gah! That's Yang's ship!
He's finally tracked me down here!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.200
Huh?

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:42.370
The fake Akafucrystal is hanging from it!
Now <i>that's </i>getting greedy!

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:47.830
Over at the Great Temple of Iskandar,
they just found out it was bogus,

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:50.250
and I bet it's a real mob scene right now!

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:55.200
This is nothing to laugh at.
We have to get out of here. Huh?

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.410
Something's coming from over that way, too.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:07.950
A space fleet? But from where?

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:10.870
The moon. It's a lunar fleet.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:12.750
The moon? You mean, Earth's moon?

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:14.870
They've come to get me.

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:20.950
I'm... the prince of the moon, after all.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:52.950
"Next time"
"#12 'Dream of the Moon, Dream of the Earth'"

00:23:52.950 --> 00:23:56.950
"Next time"
"#12 'Dream of the Moon, Dream of the Earth'"
Next time, "Dream of the Moon,
Dream of the Earth."

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:01.910
"Hatchi turns out to be the prince
of the moon kingdom"
"At long last, the Luna Guard
arrive from the moon..."

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:06.950
"And Robby is cornered
by Yang's golden <i>shachi </i>ship"
"Will the journey be seen through to the end?"
